WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.621
Not every concept needs its own table A concept
often deserves

00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:09.410
a separate entity when it has its own identity
several descriptive facts

00:00:09.687 --> 00:00:15.594
relationships to other concepts or is reused many
times For example

00:00:15.805 --> 00:00:19.068
a service has a code a name a price and may appear

00:00:19.094 --> 00:00:23.676
in many appointments That makes service a strong
candidate for its own

00:00:23.702 --> 00:00:29.357
table A simple attribute usually just describes
another entity

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:37.083
Birth date describes a patient Appointment start
time describes an appointment Quantity

00:00:37.109 --> 00:00:42.712
describes one service line When deciding ask whether
the concept

00:00:42.738 --> 00:00:47.662
needs to exist independently and be referenced by
other records If not

00:00:47.938 --> 00:00:50.978
it may be better represented as a column rather than
a separate

00:00:51.004 --> 00:00:51.438
table
